  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list (7 patients) is prepared under RBC-RAD-07. I ordered 6 of the 7 scans as booked, each linked to its appointment. I did not order the 10:00 AM scan for Jamaal Schmitt because of a severe past contrast reaction. Every patient was sent instructions, and each contrast patient has a signed chart note.\n\n- **08:00 AM, Britt Mohr (pt-0047)** – CT abdomen and pelvis with contrast ordered. He has diabetes and his last creatinine (9/24) is more than 30 days old, so I ordered a new one to be drawn before the scan.\n- **09:00 AM, Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015)** – CT abdomen and pelvis with contrast ordered. The 2019 radiology report from the day of the reaction graded it moderate. His allergy list says \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\", but the policy goes by the day-of report.\n  - Premedication ordered: prednisone 50 mg at 8 PM Sunday, 2 AM and 8 AM Monday, plus diphenhydramine 50 mg at 8 AM.\n  - He was told he needs a driver.\n  - Creatinine on 10/14 was 0.98 (eGFR 86), so no kidney prep is needed.\n- **10:00 AM, Jamaal Schmitt (pt-0048)** – No order placed, no substitute study, no premedication.\n  - The 2023 radiology report documents a severe reaction: anaphylaxis with low blood pressure and wheezing, treated with epinephrine.\n  - I sent an urgent consult message to the radiologist, Dr. Adeyemi, to decide what is done instead.\n  - I corrected his allergy record from \"mild hives\" to severe anaphylaxis.\n  - He was told not to come for a contrast scan until he hears from us.\n- **11:00 AM, Eduardo Stracke (pt-0012)** – CT abdomen and pelvis with contrast ordered. Creatinine on 10/13 was 2.85 (eGFR 25) and he is not on dialysis.\n  - Ordered 0.9% saline 500 mL IV starting at 10:00, and told him to arrive by 10:00.\n  - He takes insulin, not metformin.\n- **1:00 PM, Anisha Schuster (pt-0049)** – CT abdomen and pelvis with contrast ordered. She has diabetes, takes metformin and has no creatinine on file, so I ordered one before the scan. Metformin continues.\n- **2:00 PM, Lauren Beahan (pt-0046)** – CT abdomen and pelvis without contrast (stone protocol) ordered as booked. No prep needed.\n- **3:00 PM, Salvador Brakus (pt-0050)** – CT abdomen with contrast (adrenal protocol) ordered as booked. He has acute kidney injury: creatinine rose from 0.98 on 10/19 to 1.64 on 10/21, while on ibuprofen and vomiting.\n  - Ordered a new creatinine before the scan for the radiologist to review on the day, and saline 500 mL IV starting at 14:00.\n  - His metformin is on hold now and through at least 48 hours after the scan.\n  - A repeat creatinine is ordered for 10/28–10/30, with a task for you (due 10/30) to restart metformin only if his kidney function is back to normal.\n  - He was told to stop metformin, avoid NSAIDs and arrive by 2:00 PM.",
